00:37:49.450 --> 00:37:51.815
So had we configured the
IAM permissions correctly

00:37:51.815 --> 00:37:54.190
for that function, we wouldn't
have been able to do that.

00:37:54.190 --> 00:37:55.510
Now here you can
see what Protego

00:37:55.510 --> 00:37:56.780
sees when these things happen.

00:37:56.780 --> 00:37:59.030
So inline, this stuff
is being-- in this case,

00:37:59.030 --> 00:37:59.520
we're in alert mode.

00:37:59.520 --> 00:38:00.130
I didn't mention that.

00:38:00.130 --> 00:38:02.463
We're in alert mode, so we're
not blocking anything yet,

00:38:02.463 --> 00:38:04.420
but you can see all
the types of events

00:38:04.420 --> 00:38:05.590
that Protego is picking up.

00:38:05.590 --> 00:38:07.030
I see command
injection patterns,

00:38:07.030 --> 00:38:08.627
I see behaviors I didn't expect.

00:38:08.627 --> 00:38:10.960
All these things are being
detected and could be blocked

00:38:10.960 --> 00:38:13.230
and you could get
all that information.

00:38:13.230 --> 00:38:16.202
And then we can go and
switch that into block mode.

00:38:16.202 --> 00:38:18.160
So we switch our defense
mode on to block mode.

00:38:18.160 --> 00:38:21.190
We can then try the same
attack again, and what we'd see

00:38:21.190 --> 00:38:22.940
is that attack
wouldn't happen at all.

00:38:22.940 --> 00:38:26.080
So let's go back to
