00:39:10.460 --> 00:39:13.546
[APPLAUSE]

00:39:14.740 --> 00:39:17.240
MIKE MCDONALD: So the last thing
that I wanted to talk about

00:39:17.240 --> 00:39:19.190
was a poor developer experience.

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:20.660
So one of the
goals of serverless

00:39:20.660 --> 00:39:23.900
is to abstract away
a lot of the toil

00:39:23.900 --> 00:39:26.900
and give developers a really,
really fast way of developing.

00:39:26.900 --> 00:39:30.080
But there are still developer
experience speedblocks

00:39:30.080 --> 00:39:32.510
or roadblocks along the way.

00:39:32.510 --> 00:39:35.960
So a number of issues that we
see, particularly people using

00:39:35.960 --> 00:39:36.860
shared environments.

00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:40.010
That's a really common way to
pollute your database or leak

00:39:40.010 --> 00:39:41.930
credentials or similar
things because you're

00:39:41.930 --> 00:39:43.940
sharing that information
that really shouldn't

00:39:43.940 --> 00:39:46.310
be shared across environments.

00:39:46.310 --> 00:39:50.870
So using project boundaries
to enforce that isolation

00:39:50.870 --> 00:39:54.000
is a good developer
experience practice.

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:56.330
And using tools like
Deployment Manager or Terraform

00:39:56.330 --> 00:39:58.100
to then deploy your functions.

00:39:58.100 --> 00:40:01.430
It's really easy to just do
gCloud, functions deploy,

00:40:01.430 --> 00:40:03.560
but especially for
your production

00:40:03.560 --> 00:40:05.660
and similar environments,
you want to actually

00:40:05.660 --> 00:40:07.640
have a bunch of that automated.

00:40:07.640 --> 00:40:10.070
Which is going over
to our second side.

00:40:10.070 --> 00:40:14.090
If you have a slow toolchain,
or you're manually SCP'ing files

00:40:14.090 --> 00:40:16.970
from one place to another,
you're going to end up with

00:40:16.970 --> 00:40:19.910
security issues just because
people make mistakes.

00:40:19.910 --> 00:40:24.080
So setting up CI/CD tools, so
Spinnaker or Cloud Build, to,

00:40:24.080 --> 00:40:25.880
hey, I actually
have a couple apps

00:40:25.880 --> 00:40:30.140
that are running in the
Cloud Source editor.

00:40:30.140 --> 00:40:32.090
So I edit all of my code there.

00:40:32.090 --> 00:40:34.130
I then commit it to get repo.

00:40:34.130 --> 00:40:36.560
It's picked up automatically
by Cloud Build.

00:40:36.560 --> 00:40:39.110
Build's entirely
deployed the containers,

00:40:39.110 --> 00:40:41.390
does a traffic split, and
everything is kind of safe

00:40:41.390 --> 00:40:43.215
and I don't have
to worry about it.

00:40:43.215 --> 00:40:44.840
So I'm not manually
doing those things,

00:40:44.840 --> 00:40:47.090
and I'm not going to screw
it up because I did it once

00:40:47.090 --> 00:40:49.260
and I tested it.

00:40:49.260 --> 00:40:51.210
So we actually already
demoed, so I'm going

00:40:51.210 --> 00:40:53.453
to just leave that slide there.

